Z||000000||BJW||01-26-2001||01:49 AM||||OK. How does one get the TPS off if the bolts are seized in the throttle body?<P>One is already bustoff (like my term?)<P>the other is still seized (even with LOTS of penetrating oil . . .<P>I guess I have to remove the throttle body, drill and retap . . . <P>secondary question:<P>Anyone had any experience with the larger throttle body that I think the Fiero Store sells??<P>Thanks!<P>B in Toronto (my '87 V6 Gt is in the garage for the winter, but I DO want to fix this problem!)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Elenor84||01-26-2001||03:00 AM||||I just recently replace my tps...this did not happen to me but what I find helps is taping on the bold with something metal...to create a vibration...now tap on it vigoresltly but not to hard...its not striped is it?  If not then try to unscrew it...tap on it again and repeat...it might help...might not...just a guess...keep me posted<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
